{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/362783-gmc-freeform-tactics","id":362783,"title":"[GMC] Freeform Tactics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-07T12:23:11-08:00","id":362783,"title":"[GMC] Freeform Tactics","content":"I've kinda thought that Tactics are, as it stands, kinda impersonal. They aren't anything the <i>players</i> have a great deal of buy-in for; there's also the issue that I have players who don't have the time or inclination to pour through the books to find cool tactics. So, I've decided to write up the following, with the hopes that people can help me tweak it until usable.<br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tactics</span></div> <br /> Hunter cells are capable of incredible amounts of coordination; they need to be if they are going to last <i>any</i> amount of time on the Vigil. Tactics are this capability codified - they represent how a group of vagabonds, office workers, and soccer moms can take out ancient vampires and werewolf packs.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems:</b> A Tactic begins with an <i>Intent</i>; the players and the ST need to establish what the Tactic is intended to do. The ST then figures out a few Attribute + Skill pools; one for the Primary actor, and then one or more for the Secondary actors.<br /> <br /> Depending on the Intent of the Tactic, it may be either a normal action or an extended action, whichever makes more sense; regardless, a Tactic is <i>always</i> a Teamwork Action. The ST also decided if the effects of the Tactic are best represented by one of the following:<ul><li>Adding a Condition.</li> <li>Removing a Condition.</li> <li>The normal benefits of such an action, writ large.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Everyone's hopes and expectations were placed on the Primary Actor - and they let everyone down. The ST should adjudicate this the same way as a Failure, with an extra measure of pain for the Primary Actor.<br /> As a small comfort, the Cell takes a Practical Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> Whatever the Cell was trying, it didn't work; depending on the Intent of the Tactic, this could be anywhere from disappointing to deadly.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Tactic succeeds without a hitch; the expected recipient receives a Condition, removes a Condition, or the large-scale action succeeds.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Cell learns something about how they work together from the Tactic; as a Success, and the Cell takes a Practical Beat.<br /> <br /> <i>Learning Tactics</i><br /> A Tactic may be learned by spending 3 Practical Experience; Cells that are part of a Compact or Conspiracy may purchase Tactics that are appropriate for their Compact or Conspiracy for 2 Practical Experience instead.<br /> As a general benefit, anyone in the Cell who possesses a Speciality in the Tactic applies the benefits of the Area of Expertise and Interdisciplinary Speciality merits to that Speciality free of charge - however, this extra benefit only applies while the Hunter is a member of a Cell that knows that Tactic (it's pretty common for &quot;transplant Hunters&quot; to teach their new Cell one of their old Cell's Tactics.)<br /> <br /> <i>Ad-Libbing Tactics</i><br /> Most of the time, a Cell doesn't <i>have time</i> to practice a Tactic before they go on the hunt; twists of circumstance can leave them trying to figure out an appropriate response. In these circumstances, both the Primary Actor and the Secondary Actors take a -2 penalty on each roll made as part of the Tactic.<br /> <br /> <i>Outsiders and Tactics</i><br /> Anyone can technically help a Hunter cell with a Tactic; however, they do not have the same level of cohesion as an &quot;unbroken&quot; Cell. Non-Hunters cannot serve as the Primary Actor for a Tactic, and take a -[2 + Potency] penalty on all rolls made as part of a Tactic.<br /> <br /> <b>Transplant [Persistent]</b><br /> You came from a different Cell, and haven't won everyone in your new &quot;team&quot; over. You take a -1 penalty on all Social rolls involving your new Cell, can't serve as the Primary Actor in any Tactics, and take a -2 penalty on all rolls made as part of a Tactic.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition:</b> Joining a new Cell.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Prove that you're a part of the Cell, get drummed out of the Cell.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> N/A","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}